# erbq-event-q2.te — the point-event#1 count panel at the measured q.
# The pre-registered law (largest power of two with n/q >= 20) evaluated at the measured
# population: the OMNI_HRO_1MIN span carries only ~60 of the 198 Tohoku stamps
# (artifact field-te-count, run 37201862389: floor(n/q)=7 for q=8; the compiler carries
# no cap — omni_hro_compiler.rs harvests the full HAPI window). The q=8 seal
# `erbq-event.te` stays untouched; this is a separate, separately registered instance.
# Population named: Tohoku events within the OMNI_HRO_1MIN span, not the century.
# The q=8 plan was abandoned for infeasibility (span-limited n), not for results.
# Cost named: q=2 is a median split (df=1) — weaker evidence than q=8; any q=8 run
# on recovered events would be exploratory, not confirmatory.
pair erbq-event-q2
form event-conditional
witness point-event#1
driver omni_hro_imf_bz_gsm_nt
count quantile 2
cadence live
bin 3600
surrogate 1000
